-- Containment index over a SET physicality's member ids (PhysicalityType.Set = 5).
--
-- Separate from physicalities_constituents_gin rather than widening its `type = 1`
-- predicate. Two reasons, both structural. The text index is the most expensive one on
-- this table -- ~96% of its index-entry writes -- and admitting a second shape into it
-- would put set writes behind the same pending-list flush that the text seed already
-- saturates. And the two shapes answer different questions: a text trajectory's
-- constituent order carries sequence, while a set's does
-- not, so a probe that means "contains this token at some offset" and one that means
-- "this member is in the set" must not share a posting list.
--
-- Set identities are content-addressed, so repeated member sets reuse one physicality.
-- This index scales with distinct compositions rather than the number of attributes that
-- point at them. Pending-list tuning remains measurement-driven.
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS physicalities_set_constituents_gin
    ON physicalities USING gin (public.laplace_trajectory_constituent_ids(trajectory))
    WHERE type = 5 AND trajectory IS NOT NULL;
